guide.kg.body.guide_grill.1=A grill holds up to 3 skewers. Light it first, then insert raw skewers.
guide.kg.body.guide_grill.2=Brush with oil and flip 4 times. Add special seasoning before taking the skewer out.
guide.kg.body.guide_grill.3=Remove cooked skewers in time; continued heating overcooks them and eventually burns them into charcoal.
guide.kg.body.guide_threading.1=Hold a stick or unfinished skewer in the off hand and a skewerable ingredient in the main hand, then use it to thread one ingredient at a time.
guide.kg.body.guide_threading.2=A skewer holds up to 3 ingredients. Fixed combinations become their matching raw skewer; other combinations can become a Secret Mix Skewer.
guide.kg.body.guide_threading.3=Sneak to disassemble an uncooked handmade skewer and recover its ingredients and stick.
guide.kg.body.guide_plate.1=A skewer plate stores up to 5 skewers. Use a skewer on the plate to add it; use an empty hand to take back the last skewer.
guide.kg.body.guide_plate.2=Sneak-place a non-empty plate on a solid block or Kaleidoscope Cookery table.
guide.kg.body.guide_plate.3=Eating from the plate consumes the skewer with the highest nutrition first.
guide.kg.body.guide_crops.1=Canola, Houttuynia, Onion, and Sweet Potato can be planted and harvested, then processed further.
guide.kg.body.guide_crops.2=Canola becomes oil cake and canola oil; Houttuynia, Onion, and Sweet Potato feed into chopping, milling, or cooking chains.
guide.kg.body.guide_crops.3=Cookery Red Chili can be milled into Red Chili Powder and then used for Chili Oil.
guide.kg.body.guide_oil.1=The oil press holds up to 4 oil cakes. Fill it, then strike it repeatedly with an anvil or valid press stone to produce canola oil and oil residue.
guide.kg.body.guide_oil.2=If a compatible large vat is nearby, canola oil is deposited there first. A vat holds 8 buckets and stores one fluid type at a time.
guide.kg.body.guide_oil.3=The vat stores water, lava, and the three Grilling oils, and can fill Cookery oil pots directly.
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_book.1=Hold an empty Skewer Recipe Book in the main hand and a complete raw skewer in the off hand, then use it to record the recipe without consuming the skewer.
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_book.2=Use a recorded book with a stick in the off hand to pull ingredients from inventory and craft automatically.
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_book.3=A recorded book can also be placed on a block side; use a stick on the placed recipe for quick crafting.
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_beef.1=Ingredient order: Beef Chunks → Red Chili → Beef Chunks
guide.kg.body.guide_recipe_beef.2=Put the finished raw skewer on the grill, then oil, flip, and season it until cooked.
